  "id": "e6490078-f40f-5cec-a69a-2fea82df41e6",
  "slug": "asian-flair-flat-iron-steak",
  "name": "Asian Flair Flat Iron Steak",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "After rummaging online recipes, and experimenting with my own, I came up with this sweet and tangy sesame marinade that my husband and I find quite tasty! You can also try cooking it in your indoor (we have a Foreman) grill.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Whisk together 2 tablespoons of sesame oil with the garlic, salt, onion powder, Cajun seasoning, hot pepper sauce, soy sauce, teriyaki sauce, and brown sugar in a bowl, then pour into a resealable plastic bag. Add the flat iron steak, coat with the marinade, squeeze out excess air, and seal the bag. Marinate in the refrigerator for 12 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Remove the flat iron steak from the marinade, and shake off excess. Discard the remaining marinade. Heat the remaining 3 tablespoons of sesame oil in a cast iron skillet over medium high heat until it begins to smoke. Sear the steak in the hot oil until cooked to your desired degree of doneness, about 3 minutes per side for medium. Remove the steak from the skillet and set aside to rest for 5 minutes before slicing thinly. While the steak is resting, cook the bell pepper in the hot skillet until it begins to soften, about 1 minute. Stir in the green onions, and cook for 30 seconds more. Serve the pepper mixture over the sliced steak."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 3,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
